Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- "$f(x,y)=\sin(x)\sin(y),x\in(0,2\pi),y\in(0,2\pi)$" fused the function
  and its two domain restrictions with bare commas into one math span,
  with no prose spacing between clauses. Split into three separate math
  spans joined by prose commas, matching the file's own convention
  elsewhere in the repo (e.g. "$x=\cos(t)$, $y=\sin(t)$,
  $t\in(0,2\pi]$" in the parametric-equations exercises).
- "$(0,0),(0,4),\,\text{and}\,(5,0)$" used \text{and} with manual math
  spacing to join a list of points instead of keeping "and" as ordinary
  prose outside math mode; changed to "$(0,0)$, $(0,4)$, and $(5,0)$".
- "$R=\{(x,y){:}\,-2\le x\le2,-2\le y\le2\}$" and the similar set
  description two lines later used an empty-group-plus-colon "{:}"
  artifact from the converter instead of a plain colon, and had no
  space after the inner comma separating the two inequalities. Changed
  both to "$R=\{(x,y):\ ...,\ ...\}$".
- "$4$ ft$^{3}$" split the quantity and its unit across two math spans
  instead of typesetting the unit as \text{} inside one span, unlike
  the unit convention used throughout the rest of the repo (e.g.
  "$2\,\text{g}/\text{cm}^{2}/\text{yr}$"); changed to
  "$4\,\text{ft}^{3}$".
- "Find the values of x and y to maximize the total revenue." left the
  variables x and y as bare prose at the end of the sentence, even
  though the same sentence uses "$x$" and "$y$" earlier; wrapped both
  in math mode for consistency.

